  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nWith the system out of the area, high pressure will quickly try to \nreturn to the Panhandles and bring with it mild temperatures in the \n50s.  There is a very low chance that localized areas end up 2 to 5 \ndegrees cooler from any snow that over performs on Tuesday.  But \nwould expect any remaining snow from Tuesday to be melted by \nWednesday.  And overall it looks like a pretty easy travel day prior \nto Thanksgiving. While we remain over high pressure on Thanksgiving \nwe will cool off a bit as an upper trough dives over the Mississippi \nValley and clips the Panhandles with a weak back door cold front. As \nthe system exits on Friday through the weekend, high pressure will \nonce again take control for the Panhandles and we can expect highs \nin the upper 50s to lower 60s with mostly clear skies.  \n\nWeber",
